# Open Persona server kit: where each night's backup goes OFF the host (bin/backup.sh).
# TEMPLATE: tokens are explained in common.env.example. Never put a real value here.
#
# Read by the systemd unit open-persona-backup.service (EnvironmentFile). EMPTY (the
# default) means no off-site copy yet: the backup still runs, locally, and logs
# "off-site copy PENDING" every night. Ruling D4 (2026-11-07): the target is Azure Blob
# with an immutability policy, reached with a WRITE-ONLY SAS and age-encrypted before it
# leaves, provisioned by the Terraform session. When it exists, the owner sets a command
# that receives the night's directory as its one argument, for example a script under
# /opt/open-persona/bin that encrypts with age to a public key and uploads with the SAS.
# The decryption key never comes to this host.
OFFSITE_CMD=
